permissions.macro is vendored byte-identical to the ref above so that it can be
re-verified with a plain diff:

  curl -sSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/XRPLF/rippled/e3c8996e44921fe3b4e02c65cb41948848bcc7c5/include/xrpl/protocol/detail/permissions.macro \
    | diff - Tests/Xrpl.Tests/Fixtures/permissions.macro

Pinned to the same develop commit as transactions.macro, and for the same reason:
that is the commit the nightly stand is pinned to (.ci-config/Dockerfile.nightly),
so the fixtures and the stand describe one build. The two files are read together
anyway - a granular permission names the transaction type it applies to, and
TestUGranularPermissionConformance checks those names against transactions.macro.

This file is the only source for the granular permissions. definitions.json does
not carry them and never will: it holds fields, ledger entry types, transaction
types and results, which is why GenerateEnums cannot produce GranularPermission
the way it produces the others.

Do not hand-edit it. When protocol-watch reports a change to this file upstream,
replace it wholesale, update the sha above, and let
TestUGranularPermissionConformance show which enum members have to follow.
